sh: recover T bit and bit test code lost since GCC 9

Since GCC 9 the middle end turns some conditionals into arithmetic or
range checks that the SH patterns do not recognize, so GCC 14 and 16
generate longer code than GCC 8 for them:

1. "c ? 0x7FFFFFFF : 0x80000000" becomes "-(int) c ^ 0x80000000", which
   combine presents as C - T, and "c ? 0x80000000 : 0x7FFFFFFF" becomes
   "-(int) c ^ 0x7FFFFFFF", that is 0x7FFFFFFF + T.  GCC 8 used negc or
   addc; GCC 14 used subc, not, xor and add.  New patterns *negc_const
   and *addc_const_xor emit negc (0 - Rm - T) or addc (Rn + Rm + T),
   dropping a trailing nott of the T bit expression when there is one
   and, for 0x7FFFFFFF + T, using the opposite comparison when it is just
   as cheap.

2. "(x & ~(2^k - 1)) != 0" on a byte or halfword becomes
   "x >u 2^k - 1".  GCC 8 used "tst #imm,r0"; GCC 14 extends x (extu or
   exts) and compares with cmp/hi, two more insns.  New patterns match the
   unsigned compare of an extended or narrow byte or halfword with
   2^k - 1 and split it into a tst on the unextended value (tstsi_t),
   for <=u always and for >u when a conditional branch uses the T bit
   (sh_treg_combine inverts the branch); a stored >u result keeps cmp/hi.
   They only match before split1 (sh_pre_split1_p), so that IRA cannot
   recreate them after they can no longer be split.

Measured on sh-elf -m2 (GDB SH simulator), GCC 14.3 and 16.2 with this
patch against without it:
- Generated tests of the conditional constant forms (1,080 functions x
  229 inputs) and of byte/halfword/word bit tests (1,248 functions x 59
  values): all results correct at -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os.  Instructions at -O2:
  10,536 -> 10,419 and 38,904 -> 38,628 (14.3), 10,522 -> 10,415 and
  38,966 -> 38,770 (16.2); GCC 8.4: 10,475 and 38,946.
- gcc.target/sh: pr49263, pr49263-4 and pr51244-12 (and pr49263-1 on
  14.3) pass again, none newly fails; instructions over all its
  functions 116,493 -> 116,373 (14.3), 116,467 -> 116,372 (16.2);
  GCC 8.4: 116,343.
- GCC torture execute and compile suites, zlib and benchmarks at
  -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os: no compile failure, no change of any run result,
  .text 0.003% to 0.027% smaller, cycles unchanged.

Ported to 11.5.0: same generated tests correct at -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os,
instructions at -O2 10483 -> 10432 and 38946 -> 38762; torture execute and
compile, zlib and benchmarks at -O2/-Os: no change of any run
result, .text 0.002% (-O2) and 0.003% (-Os) smaller.

