+;; halfword, which GCC 9 and later make out of "(x & ~(2^k - 1)) != 0" and
+;; "== 0", are such tests again: "tst #imm,r0" on the unextended value
+;; instead of extu, mov #imm and cmp/hi.  See sh_split_cmpu_pow2m1.  Only
+;; before split1, and only with the extension (or the narrow mode) in the
+;; pattern, so that the constant of a plain cmp/hi is never put back into
+;; these patterns (by IRA, or by cse before loop invariant motion).
+(define_code_iterator gtu_leu [gtu leu])
